            "notes": "## Powers\n\nIn most games, I get [Bow Down](item_0673e9ed-37dd-4e58-acef-77e0fbe613fb) because you get so many ults. It has a lot of utility \u2014 for example, you can sometimes kill Kiriko before she can use Suzu, or stun Moira out of her ult. \n\nThe alternative would [Thrill of Battle](item_80ed7f65-e015-4dbb-ada0-fb8fa9b9b086) if your team stacks, then this would give you more ults.\n\n## Items\n\n[Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) is the item I get in most rounds. It\u2019s a hybrid item, so it scales your primary fire, E, ults, knife, and regular bleeds.\n\n[Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27) is solid too if you're up against a lot of armor.\n\n## IMPORTANT !\n\nAgainst heavy healing comps(so half the games), you might want to get [El-sa'ka Suppressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100). This item is already super powerful in most games. You can also sell [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) if you have the 5k for it \u2014 losing 5% WP is fine because the effect is that strong. You're already aiming for headshots anyway, and it lets you instantly apply [Royal Bullets](item_3dee6c30-86d8-4d60-b877-4d78b6a6da7c) afterwards.\n\nIf you don\u2019t go for an offensive item, then buy [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8), which is honestly just as good. The 15% mitigation makes it easier to heal back up. It also has a funny interaction with sleep dart \u2014 it wakes you up instantly because of the 5 damage from the dart, which triggers the DOT from [Nebula Conduit](item_476b7040-54c9-4f0c-8283-b4407f6809f8) and wakes you up.",
